Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:24:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hnetcfg: services, remote administration, ICMP settings,
 service restriction, UPnP edits (3189)

INetFwServices/INetFwService are real: File and Printer Sharing, UPnP Framework and Remote Desktop
(Count 3, Item, For Each, IDispatch), each backed by one of Stained Glass Firewall's built-in
groups (file-sharing, network-discovery, remote-desktop): Enabled reads the status file's group
line for the Domain network (the Domain profile) or the Private one (the Standard profile) and
changes it through sg-admind's "firewall group NAME PROFILES", refused for a standard user;
Customized compares with the group's built-in setting and the stored scope; IpVersion, Scope and
RemoteAddresses live in the profile's Services\<name> key and follow each other as for the
authorized applications; GloballyOpenPorts lists the service's ports.

INetFwProfile::RemoteAdminSettings and IcmpSettings keep their values in the profile's keys (the
Standard profile's go to Private and Public); AllowInboundEchoRequest is pushed to the firewall at
once. INetFwPolicy2::ServiceRestriction records which (service, program) pairs are restricted and
has its own Rules collection, kept in RestrictedServices\Configurable\System and never given to the
firewall. INetFwRule::Interfaces round-trips as an array of names.

IStaticPortMapping Edit*/Enable replace the gateway's entry (AddPortMapping for the same port);
IUPnPNAT::DynamicPortMappingCollection (mappings with a lease or a remote host, with
IDynamicPortMapping) and NATEventManager (callbacks kept) exist. INetFwServiceRestriction and the
two ICMP/remote-admin interfaces are in the type table; the two todo_wine in the tests now pass.

